cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "nimimo: Non-custodial crypto identity for humans"
message: >-
  If you use this software, the four-axis decomposition, or the
  sixteen-state taxonomy, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Chris
    family-names: Zemmel
    email: chris@nimimo.com
    website: "https://nimimo.com"
    affiliation: Independent
repository-code: "https://github.com/chriszemmel/nimimo-core"
url: "https://nimimo.com"
abstract: >-
  nimimo is a non-custodial cryptographic identity system that
  separates four independent axes - Access, Identity, Ownership,
  and Recovery - into distinct, replaceable layers. Keys are
  generated client-side and never transmitted to the server. The
  accompanying architecture papers introduce a sixteen-state
  taxonomy of cryptographic identity systems and formalize the
  Separated Full State (1,1,1,1) as the only configuration in
  which all four axes coexist without collapsing into each other.
keywords:
